<BaseLayout title="About Sabi Update" description="Why Sabi Update exists and how we make digital life easier to understand.">
  <section class="page-hero container"><span class="eyebrow">About</span><h1>Technology should not need translation.</h1><p>Sabi Update publishes clear, practical answers for the phones, apps, networks and online services people use every day.</p></section>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:20px"><div class="reading article-body"><h2>What we cover</h2><p>We focus on tasks and problems: changing a setting, fixing an app, understanding a digital term, checking a service, or finding the right next step when something stops working.</p><h2>What we do not want to become</h2><p>Sabi Update is not a generic technology news site. We do not publish filler simply to increase page count. The publication is organized around useful search questions, updated guides and clear explanations.</p><h2>Built for clarity</h2><p>Our default editorial rule is simple: answer the question early, show the steps clearly, explain common failure points, and state when information was last checked if the process can change.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
